  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:11211",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"The exclusion applies only while the interest equalization tax in section 4911 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1954 applies, with its period tied to the date specified in section 4911(d), which later statutes changed; the held texts include the amending orders EO 11368 and EO 11506 but no held text of the interest equalization tax extension acts or of the repeal (Public Law 94-455 is listed by the dossier as absent from the census), so the end instrument and its date are not supported. Missing sources: the text of the statute that ended the tax or repealed sections 4911 to 4920, and any order terminating the exclusion.\"]"
  },
  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:11215",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"Section 4(b) ends the Commission not later than thirty days after the date of transmittal of its final report to the President, and no held source gives that transmittal date; section 4(a) was also amended by EO 11309 (18 months changed to 20 months), which leaves the outer date at no fixed day. Missing source: a held text giving the date the final report was transmitted, or an order terminating the Commission.\"]"
  },
